  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -32,28 +32,6 @@ This release fixes an API/ABI change that was introduced in Wireshark 4.6.1, whi\n \n The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-* wssalink:2025-07[] {notable}\n-HTTP3 dissector crash.\n-wsbuglink:20860[].\n-// cveidlink:2025-xxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: 9139917bd8\n-// Fixed in release-4.6: 38df909ca8\n-// Fixed in release-4.4: 3911b2958d\n-// CVSS AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\n-// CWE-1325\n-// * HTTP/3 dissector freezes on a large number of headers. wsbuglink:20860[].\n-\n-* wssalink:2025-08[] {notable}\n-MEGACO dissector infinite loop.\n-wsbuglink:20884[].\n-// cveidlink:2025-xxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: aba1fbe626\n-// Fixed in release-4.6: 4f79070084\n-// Fixed in release-4.4: e4f3706e1b\n-// AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\n-// CWE-835\n-// * Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-11-30-12267984256.pcap. wsbuglink:20884[].\n-\n // * wssalink:2025-09[] {notable}\n // Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n // wsbuglink:xxx[].\n@@ -72,18 +50,9 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n // Bugs with the {notable} attribute show up in the \"What's Changed\" box on the download page.\n //* Wireshark contains traces of nuts. What kind of nuts? The kind you're allergic to. wsbuglink:5000[] {notable}\n \n-* ws_base32_decode should be named *_encode ? wsbuglink:20754[].\n-* Omnipeek files not working in 4.6.1. wsbuglink:20876[].\n-* Stack buffer overflow in wiretap/ber.c (ber_open) wsbuglink:20878[].\n-* Plugins incompatibility between 4.6.0 & 4.6.1. wsbuglink:20881[]. {notable}\n-* Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-11-30-12266121180.pcap. wsbuglink:20883[].\n-\n // == Known Bugs\n \n-=== New and Updated Features\n-\n-* The Windows installers now ship with the Visual C++ Redistributable version 14.44.35112.\n-  They previously shipped with 14.40.33807.\n+// === New and Updated Features\n \n // === Removed Features and Support\n \n@@ -99,36 +68,15 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // rg -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.6.2.. | rg packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-ATM PW\n-COSEM\n-COTP\n-DECT NR+\n-DMP\n-Fc00\n-GTP\n-HTTP3\n-IEEE 802.15.4\n-ISIS HELLO\n-ISOBUS\n-MAC-LTE\n-MAUSB\n-MEGACO\n-MPEG DSM-CC\n-OsmoTRXD\n-PTP\n-SAPDIAG\n-SMTP\n-RLC\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-[commaize]\n---\n-Peektagged\n---\n+// [commaize]\n+// --\n+// --\n \n === New and Updated File Format Decoding Support\n \n@@ -152,6 +100,30 @@ There is no new or updated file format support in this release.\n \n == Prior Versions\n \n+Wireshark 4.6.2 included the following changes.\n+See the\n+https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.6.2.html[release notes]\n+for details:\n+\n+This release fixes an API/ABI change that was introduced in Wireshark 4.6.1, which caused a compatibility issue with plugins built for Wireshark 4.6.0. wsbuglink:20881[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2025-07[] {notable}\n+HTTP3 dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:20860[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2025-08[] {notable}\n+MEGACO dissector infinite loop.\n+wsbuglink:20884[].\n+\n+* ws_base32_decode should be named *_encode ? wsbuglink:20754[].\n+* Omnipeek files not working in 4.6.1. wsbuglink:20876[].\n+* Stack buffer overflow in wiretap/ber.c (ber_open) wsbuglink:20878[].\n+* Plugins incompatibility between 4.6.0 & 4.6.1. wsbuglink:20881[]. {notable}\n+* Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-11-30-12266121180.pcap. wsbuglink:20883[].\n+\n+* The Windows installers now ship with the Visual C++ Redistributable version 14.44.35112.\n+  They previously shipped with 14.40.33807.\n+\n Wireshark 4.6.1 included the following changes.\n See the\n https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.6.1.html[release notes]\n",
      "collapsed": false,
